/* 15 天题库：150 题（英语 75 / 数学 45 / 语文 30）*/
window.DAYS = [{"day":1,"title":"摸底：先看清自己的起点","minutes":30,"focus":["英语词汇","四则运算","语文基础"],"warmup":"第一天不看速度，只看「错在哪」。做完把错题按科目记一笔，明天开始前重讲一遍。","passage":{"title":"The Amazing Journey of Monarch Butterflies","text":"Every autumn, millions of monarch butterflies leave Canada and the northern United States. They fly south, sometimes more than 3,000 miles, to the mountains of central Mexico. No single butterfly makes the whole trip alone. Instead, several generations take turns, and the last group arrives in Mexico in late October.\n\nHow do they find the way? Monarchs use the sun and the earth's magnetic field. They also follow the same routes their parents used, even though they have never flown them before. Scientists call this ability instinct — something an animal knows how to do without being taught.\n\nIn spring, the butterflies fly north again. They stop to lay eggs on milkweed plants. The eggs become caterpillars, then butterflies. By summer, a new generation is ready to start the journey all over again.","note":"先通读一遍，再做题。读的时候把数字和地点圈出来——细节题都藏在这些地方。"},"questions":[{"subject":"eng","skill":"词汇","type":"choice","stem":"The word \"enormous\" most nearly means —","options":["very small","very large","very fast","very old"],"answer":1,"explain":"enormous = 巨大的。近义替换题先看词根：e-（向外）+ norm（标准）→ 超出常规尺寸。"},{"subject":"eng","skill":"反义词","type":"choice","stem":"Which word is the OPPOSITE of \"generous\"?","options":["kind","selfish","wealthy","brave"],"answer":1,"explain":"generous 慷慨的；selfish 自私的。kind 善良、wealthy 富有、brave 勇敢，都不构成反义。"},{"subject":"eng","skill":"主旨","type":"reading","stem":"What is the main idea of the passage?","options":["Monarch butterflies are the most beautiful butterflies in North America.","Monarch butterflies make a long yearly journey that no single butterfly completes alone.","Monarch butterflies live only in the mountains of Mexico.","Scientists are trying to stop monarch butterflies from flying south."],"answer":1,"explain":"主旨题看首段和末段：全文讲「迁徙 + 几代接力完成」，B 正好概括。A 是文中没提的评价，C 与原文矛盾（还分布在加拿大、美国），D 无中生有。"},{"subject":"eng","skill":"细节","type":"reading","stem":"According to the passage, how do monarchs find their way south?","options":["They follow rivers and roads.","They use the sun and the earth's magnetic field.","They follow other kinds of butterflies.","They remember the trip from last year."],"answer":1,"explain":"第二段第二句原句定位：use the sun and the earth's magnetic field。D 是典型陷阱——文中说它们走父母走过的路线，但「从未飞过」，所以不是「记得」。"},{"subject":"eng","skill":"词义猜测","type":"reading","stem":"The word \"instinct\" in the passage means —","options":["a skill an animal is born with","a place where butterflies rest","a type of plant","a long journey"],"answer":0,"explain":"原文紧跟解释：something an animal knows how to do without being taught —— 不用教就会的本领，即「本能」。"},{"subject":"math","skill":"大数加法","type":"choice","stem":"4,507 + 2,896 = ?","options":["6,393","7,303","7,403","7,413"],"answer":2,"explain":"4,507 + 2,896：个位 7+6=13 写 3 进 1；十位 0+9+1=10 写 0 进 1；百位 5+8+1=14 写 4 进 1；千位 4+2+1=7 → 7,403。"},{"subject":"math","skill":"乘法应用","type":"choice","stem":"A school buys 24 boxes of pencils. Each box has 36 pencils. How many pencils does the school buy in all?","options":["324","764","864","1,024"],"answer":2,"explain":"24 × 36 = 24 × 30 + 24 × 6 = 720 + 144 = 864。"},{"subject":"math","skill":"小数比较","type":"choice","stem":"Which number is the greatest?","options":["0.6","0.06","0.65","0.506"],"answer":2,"explain":"补齐位数再比：0.600 / 0.060 / 0.650 / 0.506。整数部分都是 0，比十分位：6、0、6、5 → 排除 0.06、0.506；再比百分位 0 vs 5 → 0.65 最大。"},{"subject":"chi","skill":"字音","type":"choice","stem":"「成长」的「长」应读作：","options":["cháng","zhǎng","zhàng","chǎng"],"answer":1,"explain":"「成长」表示生长、长大，读 zhǎng；「长短、长江」才读 cháng。多音字要按词义定音。"},{"subject":"chi","skill":"字形","type":"choice","stem":"下列词语中，没有错别字的一项是：","options":["再接再励","一丝不苟","迫不急待","兴高彩烈"],"answer":1,"explain":"应为：再接再厉（厉，磨砺）、迫不及待（及，来得及）、兴高采烈（采，神采）。只有「一丝不苟」正确。"}],"output":{"type":"口语","title":"英文自我介绍 60 秒","prompt":"用 8–10 句介绍自己：名字、几年级、住在哪里、最喜欢的科目和原因、一个爱好、一件最近做的事。录下来回听一遍。","checklist":["不看稿也能说完","每句都有主语和动词","至少用了 1 个 because 说明原因","语速不快，句末有停顿"]}},{"day":2,"title":"记叙文：把故事读成一条线","minutes":32,"focus":["名词复数与冠词","记叙文阅读","除法与估算"],"warmup":"今天读故事时，用铅笔标出三样东西：谁（who）、发生了什么（what）、最后怎样（end）。","passage":{"title":"The Lost Lunchbox","text":"Mia opened her backpack and froze. Her lunchbox was gone. Inside it was the dumplings her grandmother had made that morning, wrapped in a red cloth. Mia had been waiting for lunch all day.\n\nAt noon, she walked slowly to the cafeteria. She looked under every table, but there was nothing. Then she heard a small voice behind her. \"Is this yours?\" A boy in a blue jacket was holding a red cloth bundle. \"I found it near the water fountain. I think someone left it there by mistake.\"\n\nMia's face turned red. She had left it there herself, after washing her hands. \"Thank you,\" she said. \"Do you want to share? My grandma always makes too many.\"\n\nThe boy smiled. His name was Leo, and he had just moved to the school that week.","note":"记叙文四要素：人物、地点、问题、结局。读完先在心里复述一遍这条线，再动笔答题。"},"questions":[{"subject":"eng","skill":"名词复数","type":"choice","stem":"One child, two ______.","options":["childs","childes","children","childrens"],"answer":2,"explain":"child 的复数是不规则变化 children，不能再加 s。同类：man→men, woman→women, foot→feet, tooth→teeth。"},{"subject":"eng","skill":"冠词","type":"choice","stem":"My brother is ______ honest boy.","options":["a","an","the","（不填）"],"answer":1,"explain":"看读音不看字母：honest 的 h 不发音，首音是元音 /ɒ/，所以用 an。同类：an hour, a university。"},{"subject":"eng","skill":"细节","type":"reading","stem":"Why did Mia freeze when she opened her backpack?","options":["She saw a note from her teacher.","She found that her lunchbox was missing.","She forgot to bring her homework.","She saw a boy in a blue jacket."],"answer":1,"explain":"首句即答案：Her lunchbox was gone。freeze 在这里是「愣住」，不是「结冰」。"},{"subject":"eng","skill":"因果","type":"reading","stem":"Why did Mia's face turn red?","options":["She was angry with Leo.","She realized she had left the lunchbox at the fountain herself.","She was hot from running.","She forgot her grandmother's name."],"answer":1,"explain":"第三段第一句后紧跟解释：She had left it there herself —— 是「不好意思」，不是生气。"},{"subject":"eng","skill":"人物推断","type":"reading","stem":"What can we learn about Leo?","options":["He had been at the school for many years.","He was new to the school and helpful.","He took the lunchbox on purpose.","He did not like dumplings."],"answer":1,"explain":"末句说他「那周才转来」，加上主动归还饭盒，可推断「新来的、友善」。推断题必须能从原文找到两个依据。"},{"subject":"math","skill":"除法余数","type":"choice","stem":"What is the remainder when 137 is divided by 6?","options":["3","5","22","23"],"answer":1,"explain":"6 × 22 = 132，137 − 132 = 5，余数 5。注意 22 是商不是余数，别选错。"},{"subject":"math","skill":"估算","type":"choice","stem":"A school has 19 buses. Each bus holds 48 students. ABOUT how many students can ride at once?","options":["500","800","1,000","1,200"],"answer":2,"explain":"估算把 19 看成 20、48 看成 50：20 × 50 = 1,000。题目问 about，不需要精确计算 912。"},{"subject":"math","skill":"除法应用","type":"choice","stem":"A book has 168 pages. Tom reads 24 pages a day. How many days will he need to finish the book?","options":["6","7","8","9"],"answer":1,"explain":"168 ÷ 24 = 7。验算：24 × 7 = 168。"},{"subject":"chi","skill":"量词","type":"choice","stem":"下列量词使用正确的一项是：","options":["一匹马","一条牛","一头马","一只牛"],"answer":0,"explain":"马用「匹」，牛用「头」。量词是固定搭配，读的时候要整体记，不要靠推理。"},{"subject":"chi","skill":"近义词","type":"choice","stem":"「高兴」的近义词是：","options":["难过","愉快","生气","着急"],"answer":1,"explain":"高兴 = 愉快、欢喜。其余三个都是相反或无关的情绪词。"}],"output":{"type":"写作","title":"英文小故事 5 句","prompt":"写一件今天真实发生的小事，用 5 句话：第 1 句交代时间地点，第 2–3 句写发生了什么，第 4 句写你的感受，第 5 句写结果。必须用过去时。","checklist":["5 句都用了过去式动词","有一句用了 because 或 but","每句首字母大写、句末有标点","没有把 go 写成 goed"]}},{"day":3,"title":"信息类阅读：作者为什么写这篇","minutes":33,"focus":["一般现在时","说明文阅读","乘法与分数比较"],"warmup":"信息类文章的结构通常是：现象 → 原因 → 但是/局限。今天重点找那个「但是」。","passage":{"title":"Robots on the Farm","text":"Robots are moving from factories to farms. In some countries, small robots already pick strawberries, pull weeds, and even plant seeds. One robot in Japan can pick a strawberry every eight seconds. It uses a camera to find fruit that is red and ripe, and it never damages the plant.\n\nFarmers say the machines help them in two ways. First, robots can work all night, when it is cooler and the fruit stays fresh longer. Second, they solve a serious problem: fewer young people want to work on farms.\n\nBut robots are not perfect. They are expensive, and they cannot fix a broken water pipe or decide which field needs rain. For now, most farmers use robots as helpers, not as replacements for people.","note":"注意最后一段的 But —— 凡是出现转折词，后面几乎一定有一道题。"},"questions":[{"subject":"eng","skill":"一般现在时","type":"choice","stem":"My sister ______ to school by bus every day.","options":["go","goes","going","gone"],"answer":1,"explain":"every day 是一般现在时标志；主语 My sister 是第三人称单数，动词加 -es → goes。"},{"subject":"eng","skill":"语序","type":"choice","stem":"Choose the sentence that is written correctly.","options":["He always is late for class.","He is always late for class.","Always he is late for class.","He is late always for class."],"answer":1,"explain":"频度副词 always 放在 be 动词之后、实义动词之前：He is always late. / He always comes late."},{"subject":"eng","skill":"主旨","type":"reading","stem":"What is the main idea of the passage?","options":["Robots will soon replace all farm workers.","Robots are useful helpers on farms, but they cannot do everything.","Strawberries are the most important crop in Japan.","Farming is easier than working in a factory."],"answer":1,"explain":"第一段讲「有什么用」，第三段 But 讲「做不到什么」，合起来就是 B。A 与结尾 not replacements 直接矛盾。"},{"subject":"eng","skill":"细节","type":"reading","stem":"According to the passage, why is picking fruit at night a good idea?","options":["Robots can see better in the dark.","The fruit stays fresh longer in cooler air.","Farmers sleep during the day.","There are fewer insects at night."],"answer":1,"explain":"原句：robots can work all night, when it is cooler and the fruit stays fresh longer。答案就在 when 从句里。"},{"subject":"eng","skill":"词义猜测","type":"reading","stem":"The word \"ripe\" is closest in meaning to —","options":["ready to be eaten","still green","very expensive","easy to find"],"answer":0,"explain":"原文说机器人找「red and ripe」的草莓，红色说明成熟可摘。ripe = 成熟的。"},{"subject":"math","skill":"乘法","type":"choice","stem":"25 × 16 = ?","options":["300","400","410","500"],"answer":1,"explain":"拆开算：25 × 16 = 25 × 4 × 4 = 100 × 4 = 400。也可以用 25 × 16 = 25 × 10 + 25 × 6 = 250 + 150 = 400。"},{"subject":"math","skill":"分数比较","type":"choice","stem":"Which fraction is greater?","options":["3/5","2/3","They are equal","It cannot be decided"],"answer":1,"explain":"通分：3/5 = 9/15，2/3 = 10/15，所以 2/3 大。也可以和 0.6 比：3/5 = 0.6，2/3 ≈ 0.67。"},{"subject":"math","skill":"时间计算","type":"choice","stem":"A movie starts at 6:45 p.m. and lasts 1 hour 40 minutes. What time does it end?","options":["8:15 p.m.","8:25 p.m.","8:35 p.m.","8:45 p.m."],"answer":1,"explain":"6:45 + 1 小时 = 7:45；7:45 + 40 分钟 = 8:25 p.m.。分两步加，别一次心算。"},{"subject":"chi","skill":"成语","type":"choice","stem":"「画蛇添足」这个成语的意思是：","options":["做事多此一举，反而不好","画画非常生动","蛇长了很多只脚","做事速度很快"],"answer":0,"explain":"出自《战国策》：给蛇画脚，本来赢了却输了。比喻做了多余的事，反而把事情弄坏。"},{"subject":"chi","skill":"多音字","type":"choice","stem":"「他在银行工作」中的「行」应读作：","options":["xíng","háng","xìng","hèng"],"answer":1,"explain":"「银行、行业、一行字」读 háng；「行走、行动、不行」读 xíng。"}],"output":{"type":"写作","title":"三句话概括一篇新闻","prompt":"找一篇适合孩子的英文短新闻（科普或动物类），读完后用三句话写摘要：第 1 句讲主题，第 2 句讲最重要的细节，第 3 句讲「所以呢」。","checklist":["三句都用完整句","没有照抄原文整句","第 3 句是自己想的","生词查过并抄进词汇本"]}},{"day":4,"title":"记叙文：人物的心里在想什么","minutes":33,"focus":["一般过去时","人物情感推断","分数与单位换算"],"warmup":"推断题不能选「原文原句」，要选「原文推出来的一句」。今天每道推断题都回原文划依据。","passage":{"title":"The First Time I Raised My Hand","text":"For three weeks, I sat at the back of the classroom and said nothing. I understood the lessons, but my words seemed to hide somewhere behind my teeth.\n\nOn a Tuesday morning, Ms. Chen asked who could explain why leaves change color. I knew the answer. My heart was beating fast, but I slowly raised my hand. It was only half up, and my fingers were shaking.\n\n\"Mia?\" she said.\n\nI stood up and spoke. My voice was small and it cracked in the middle. But I finished. Nobody laughed. Ms. Chen nodded and said, \"That is exactly right.\"\n\nAfter class, a boy named Sam came over. \"I wanted to answer too,\" he said, \"but I was too scared.\" We both laughed.\n\nNow I raise my hand almost every day. It never gets easy — but it does get easier.","note":"标出所有描写身体反应的句子（heart beating、fingers shaking、voice cracked），这些都在暗示情绪。"},"questions":[{"subject":"eng","skill":"一般过去时","type":"choice","stem":"Yesterday we ______ a great movie at the cinema.","options":["see","saw","seen","seeing"],"answer":1,"explain":"Yesterday 是过去时标志，see 的过去式是 saw（不规则动词）。"},{"subject":"eng","skill":"不规则动词","type":"choice","stem":"Choose the sentence that is written correctly.","options":["She goed to the park yesterday.","She went to the park yesterday.","She gone to the park yesterday.","She go to the park yesterday."],"answer":1,"explain":"go 的过去式是 went，不是 goed。gone 是过去分词，必须和 have/has 连用。"},{"subject":"eng","skill":"推理","type":"reading","stem":"Why did the writer sit at the back and say nothing?","options":["She did not understand the lessons.","She was afraid to speak in class.","She did not like Ms. Chen.","She was new to the school."],"answer":1,"explain":"原文说 I understood the lessons, but my words seemed to hide —— 听懂了，但说不出口，所以是「害怕开口」。A 与原文直接矛盾。"},{"subject":"eng","skill":"细节推断","type":"reading","stem":"What does \"my voice ... cracked in the middle\" tell us?","options":["She was singing a song.","She was very nervous.","She had a bad cold.","She was shouting loudly."],"answer":1,"explain":"crack 指声音发抖、破音，配合前文 fingers were shaking，都在写紧张。"},{"subject":"eng","skill":"主题","type":"reading","stem":"What is the message of this story?","options":["Leaves change color in autumn.","Doing something scary once makes it easier next time.","Teachers should not ask questions in class.","It is better to stay quiet in class."],"answer":1,"explain":"结尾点题：It never gets easy — but it does get easier。主题句常在最后一段。"},{"subject":"math","skill":"同分母分数加法","type":"choice","stem":"3/8 + 2/8 = ?","options":["5/16","5/8","6/8","1/8"],"answer":1,"explain":"同分母分数相加，分母不变、分子相加：3/8 + 2/8 = 5/8。分母不能相加，这是最常见的错。"},{"subject":"math","skill":"小数加法","type":"choice","stem":"12.6 + 3.75 = ?","options":["16.35","15.35","16.01","15.01"],"answer":0,"explain":"小数点对齐：12.60 + 3.75 = 16.35。把 12.6 补成 12.60 就不会错位。"},{"subject":"math","skill":"单位换算","type":"choice","stem":"A rope is 3.5 meters long. How many centimeters is that?","options":["35 cm","350 cm","3,500 cm","30.5 cm"],"answer":1,"explain":"1 m = 100 cm，所以 3.5 × 100 = 350 cm。大单位换小单位是乘，小数点右移两位。"},{"subject":"chi","skill":"病句","type":"choice","stem":"下列句子没有语病的一项是：","options":["我们要养成认真读书。","他穿着一件红上衣和一顶蓝帽子。","通过这次活动，我明白了合作的重要。","教室里响起了热烈的歌声。"],"answer":2,"explain":"A 缺宾语（养成……的习惯）；B 搭配不当（不能「穿」帽子）；D 搭配不当（热烈的掌声 / 嘹亮的歌声）。"},{"subject":"chi","skill":"关联词","type":"choice","stem":"（　）明天下雨，我们（　）照常出发。","options":["因为……所以","即使……也","不但……而且","如果……就"],"answer":1,"explain":"前后是「让步」关系：就算下雨，也不改变出发。选「即使……也」。「如果……就」表示条件，语气不符。"}],"output":{"type":"口语","title":"讲一个「我紧张过」的故事","prompt":"用英文讲 60–90 秒：什么时候、发生什么、身体有什么反应、最后怎么解决。要求用上 3 个情绪词（nervous / worried / proud / relieved）。","checklist":["有开头、经过、结尾","用了过去时","至少 3 个情绪词","讲完能回答家长的一个追问"]}},{"day":5,"title":"比较级最高级 + 健康类文章","minutes":33,"focus":["比较级/最高级","因果与细节","周长与平均数"],"warmup":"今天起把错题本用起来：错的题抄题号 + 一句「我为什么错」，不要抄整道题。","passage":{"title":"Why Breakfast Matters","text":"Your body is like a car. After a long night, its tank is almost empty. Breakfast is the fuel that gets you moving again.\n\nWhen you skip breakfast, your brain has less energy. You may find it harder to listen, remember, and solve problems. Studies of school children show that those who eat a healthy breakfast often pay attention better in the first classes of the day.\n\nBut not all breakfasts are equal. A bowl of sugary cereal may make you feel full for only an hour. Oats with milk, an egg, and a piece of fruit give you energy that lasts much longer, because they contain protein and fiber.\n\nYou do not need a big meal. Ten minutes is enough. What you need is something simple, and the habit of eating it every day.","note":"说明文里的比喻（body is like a car）通常对应一道「作者为什么这样写」的题。"},"questions":[{"subject":"eng","skill":"比较级","type":"choice","stem":"This book is ______ than that one.","options":["interesting","more interesting","most interesting","the most interesting"],"answer":1,"explain":"than 是比较级标志；interesting 是多音节词，比较级用 more + 原级。"},{"subject":"eng","skill":"最高级","type":"choice","stem":"Mount Everest is the ______ mountain in the world.","options":["high","higher","highest","most high"],"answer":2,"explain":"in the world 表示范围，用最高级 the highest。单音节词直接加 -est，不用 most。"},{"subject":"eng","skill":"写作目的","type":"reading","stem":"Why does the writer compare the body to a car?","options":["To explain that breakfast is fuel for the body.","To show that cars need gasoline.","To say that children should not drive.","To describe how fast the body moves."],"answer":0,"explain":"比喻是为了让读者理解抽象概念：车要加油，身体要吃早饭。答案紧跟在比喻后面一句。"},{"subject":"eng","skill":"细节","type":"reading","stem":"According to the passage, what may happen when you skip breakfast?","options":["You feel stronger in class.","It is harder to listen and remember.","You sleep better at night.","You want to eat more fruit."],"answer":1,"explain":"第二段原句：You may find it harder to listen, remember, and solve problems。"},{"subject":"eng","skill":"因果","type":"reading","stem":"Why is oats with milk a better breakfast than sugary cereal?","options":["It tastes much sweeter.","It is cheaper to buy.","Its energy lasts much longer.","It takes more time to make."],"answer":2,"explain":"第三段最后一句：give you energy that lasts much longer, because they contain protein and fiber。because 后面就是原因。"},{"subject":"math","skill":"周长","type":"choice","stem":"A rectangle is 8 cm long and 5 cm wide. What is its perimeter?","options":["13 cm","26 cm","40 cm","40 cm²"],"answer":1,"explain":"周长 = (长 + 宽) × 2 = (8 + 5) × 2 = 26 cm。注意单位是 cm，不是 cm²——cm² 是面积单位。"},{"subject":"math","skill":"角度","type":"choice","stem":"A straight line is 180°. One angle on it is 35°. What is the other angle?","options":["55°","145°","65°","125°"],"answer":1,"explain":"平角 = 180°，180° − 35° = 145°。55° 是「互余」（90° − 35°），别混。"},{"subject":"math","skill":"平均数","type":"choice","stem":"Jake read 5, 7, 4, 4 and 10 books in five months. What is the mean number of books?","options":["5","6","7","8"],"answer":1,"explain":"先求和：5+7+4+4+10 = 30；再除以个数 5：30 ÷ 5 = 6。平均数 = 总数 ÷ 份数。"},{"subject":"chi","skill":"古诗","type":"choice","stem":"「床前明月光」的下一句是：","options":["疑是地上霜","举头望明月","低头思故乡","春眠不觉晓"],"answer":0,"explain":"李白《静夜思》：床前明月光，疑是地上霜。举头望明月，低头思故乡。"},{"subject":"chi","skill":"字义","type":"choice","stem":"「一丝不苟」中「苟」的意思是：","options":["随便、马虎","认真、仔细","小狗","如果"],"answer":0,"explain":"苟 = 苟且、随便。一丝不苟形容做事十分认真，一点儿也不马虎。"}],"output":{"type":"写作","title":"英文观点段：早饭该不该吃","prompt":"写 4 句话：观点 1 句 + 理由 2 句（用 because / for example）+ 结论 1 句。不超过 60 词，句子要短。","checklist":["第一句直接给观点","两个理由不重复","用了 because 或 for example","没有一句话超过 12 个词"]}},{"day":6,"title":"说明文：跟着顺序读过程","minutes":34,"focus":["介词","水循环说明文","面积与单位"],"warmup":"过程类文章先找顺序词（first / then / when / after），把每一步编号写下来，题目就不会乱。","passage":{"title":"Where Rain Comes From","text":"Have you ever wondered where rain comes from? It begins in the ocean. The sun heats the water, and some of it turns into vapor — a gas you cannot see. This step is called evaporation.\n\nThe vapor rises into the sky. High above, the air is cold, so the vapor turns back into tiny drops of water. These drops gather around dust and form clouds. This step is called condensation.\n\nInside a cloud, the tiny drops bump into each other and become bigger. When they are too heavy to stay in the air, they fall as rain, snow, or hail.\n\nThe water then flows into rivers, lakes, and back to the ocean. The same water has been moving in this circle for millions of years. The water you drink today may once have been drunk by a dinosaur.","note":"把 evaporation、condensation、fall 三个步骤按顺序标在纸上，再看题目。"},"questions":[{"subject":"eng","skill":"介词","type":"choice","stem":"The class starts ______ 8 o'clock ______ Monday morning.","options":["at / on","on / in","in / at","at / in"],"answer":0,"explain":"具体时刻用 at（at 8 o'clock）；具体某一天或某天的上下午用 on（on Monday morning）。in 用于月份、年份、季节。"},{"subject":"eng","skill":"介词","type":"choice","stem":"The cat is hiding ______ the table, so we cannot see it.","options":["on","under","in","at"],"answer":1,"explain":"看不见 → 在桌子下面，用 under。on 是在表面上，in 是在里面。"},{"subject":"eng","skill":"主旨","type":"reading","stem":"What is the main purpose of this passage?","options":["To explain how water moves in a cycle.","To describe the ocean in summer.","To tell a story about a dinosaur.","To teach readers how to make rain."],"answer":0,"explain":"全文按 evaporation → condensation → fall → flow back 的顺序讲水循环，首尾都在说「同一个圆」。"},{"subject":"eng","skill":"顺序细节","type":"reading","stem":"What happens right AFTER vapor rises into cold air?","options":["It turns back into tiny drops of water.","It falls as snow.","It flows into rivers.","It becomes dust."],"answer":0,"explain":"第二段：the air is cold, so the vapor turns back into tiny drops of water。so 后面就是结果。"},{"subject":"eng","skill":"词义猜测","type":"reading","stem":"\"Condensation\" is the step in which —","options":["water turns into vapor","vapor turns into tiny water drops","rain falls to the ground","rivers flow into the sea"],"answer":1,"explain":"原文直接定义：the vapor turns back into tiny drops of water. This step is called condensation。词义题先在前后句找定义。"},{"subject":"math","skill":"正方形面积","type":"choice","stem":"A square has a side of 9 cm. What is its area?","options":["36 cm²","81 cm²","18 cm²","90 cm²"],"answer":1,"explain":"正方形面积 = 边长 × 边长 = 9 × 9 = 81 cm²。36 是周长（9×4），别混。"},{"subject":"math","skill":"单位换算","type":"choice","stem":"2 kilograms = ______ grams","options":["200 g","2,000 g","20,000 g","20 g"],"answer":1,"explain":"1 kg = 1,000 g，2 × 1,000 = 2,000 g。"},{"subject":"math","skill":"周长应用","type":"choice","stem":"A rectangular garden is 12 m long and 7 m wide. How much fence is needed to go all the way around it?","options":["19 m","38 m","84 m","84 m²"],"answer":1,"explain":"围一圈 = 周长 = (12 + 7) × 2 = 38 m。84 是面积（12×7），单位也不对。"},{"subject":"chi","skill":"标点","type":"choice","stem":"下列句子标点使用正确的一项是：","options":["我最喜欢的书是「西游记」。","他问我：“你去哪儿？”","花园里开满了花、有桃花、杏花、梨花。","今天天气真好啊？"],"answer":1,"explain":"A 书名应用《西游记》；C 顿号不能用在「花、有」之间，应改成冒号；D 感叹句应用叹号。B 引号内是完整问句，问号在引号内。"},{"subject":"chi","skill":"词语搭配","type":"choice","stem":"下列词语搭配不恰当的一项是：","options":["增强信心","提高水平","改善方法","养成习惯"],"answer":2,"explain":"「改善」多搭配生活、条件、环境；「方法」应与「改进」搭配。"}],"output":{"type":"写作","title":"用 4 句话写一个过程","prompt":"选一个你熟悉的流程（泡一杯茶 / 做一次手工 / 植物怎么喝水），用 first、next、then、finally 四步写清楚。","checklist":["四个顺序词都用上","每步只写一件事","动词用一般现在时","读给家长听，对方能照着做出来"]}},{"day":7,"title":"第 1 周周测：限时 25 分钟","minutes":35,"focus":["综合复习","限时训练","错题复盘"],"warmup":"今天开始计时，25 分钟内做完，做不完也停笔。真实考试里，「做得完」本身就是一项能力。","passage":{"title":"The Kite That Would Not Fly","text":"Kenji built a kite from bamboo sticks and old newspaper. He painted two red eyes on it, because his kite was going to be a dragon.\n\nOn Saturday, he took it to the hill behind his house. The wind was strong. He ran, and the kite lifted — then turned over and dived into the grass. He tried again. It crashed again.\n\nHis grandfather watched from a bench. \"Show me your tail,\" he said. Kenji's kite had no tail. \"A kite needs something to pull it back,\" his grandfather said. \"Otherwise it just spins.\"\n\nKenji tied a long strip of cloth to the bottom. This time the kite rose, shook once, and climbed steadily into the sky.\n\n\"Everything that flies,\" his grandfather said, \"needs something to hold it steady.\"","note":"限时阅读：先看题干关键词，再回原文定位，不要从头逐字读第二遍。"},"questions":[{"subject":"eng","skill":"代词","type":"choice","stem":"This is my sister. ______ name is Amy.","options":["His","Her","She","Hers"],"answer":1,"explain":"空格后是名词 name，要用形容词性物主代词 her（她的）。She 是主格，不能修饰名词。"},{"subject":"eng","skill":"代词","type":"choice","stem":"Tom and I are friends. ______ play football together every Sunday.","options":["They","We","Us","Our"],"answer":1,"explain":"Tom and I 合起来是「我们」，句中作主语用主格 We。"},{"subject":"eng","skill":"问题与解决","type":"reading","stem":"What was Kenji's problem at first?","options":["He had no wind.","His kite kept crashing.","His grandfather took his kite.","He forgot to paint the eyes."],"answer":1,"explain":"第二段连说两次失败：turned over and dived / It crashed again。"},{"subject":"eng","skill":"因果","type":"reading","stem":"Why did the kite fly after Kenji added a tail?","options":["The tail made the kite heavier.","The tail kept the kite from spinning.","The wind became stronger.","The kite became a real dragon."],"answer":1,"explain":"爷爷的话：A kite needs something to pull it back. Otherwise it just spins。「otherwise」反过来说明尾巴防止打转。"},{"subject":"eng","skill":"句意推断","type":"reading","stem":"What does the grandfather's last sentence suggest?","options":["Only kites need help.","Steadiness matters for anything that rises.","Flying is dangerous.","Children should listen to old people."],"answer":1,"explain":"Everything that flies needs something to hold it steady —— 由风筝推到「任何要飞起来的东西」，都需要让它稳的东西。"},{"subject":"math","skill":"日历推算","type":"choice","stem":"If today is Wednesday, what day of the week will it be in 10 days?","options":["Friday","Saturday","Sunday","Monday"],"answer":1,"explain":"一周 7 天，10 = 7 + 3，相当于往后推 3 天：Wed → Thu → Fri → Sat。答案是 Saturday。"},{"subject":"math","skill":"混合运算","type":"choice","stem":"36 ÷ 6 + 4 × 5 = ?","options":["26","30","50","20"],"answer":0,"explain":"先乘除后加减：36 ÷ 6 = 6，4 × 5 = 20，6 + 20 = 26。从左往右算会得到 50，那是错的。"},{"subject":"math","skill":"分数应用","type":"choice","stem":"A pizza is cut into 8 equal slices. Ben eats 3 slices. What fraction of the pizza is left?","options":["3/8","5/8","1/2","3/5"],"answer":1,"explain":"剩下 8 − 3 = 5 片，总共 8 片 → 5/8。问的是「剩下」，不是「吃掉」。"},{"subject":"chi","skill":"字义","type":"choice","stem":"「再接再厉」中「厉」的意思是：","options":["严厉","磨快、奋勉","厉害","经历"],"answer":1,"explain":"「厉」同「砺」，磨刀石，引申为磨炼、奋勉。成语指一次又一次地继续努力。"},{"subject":"chi","skill":"句子排序","type":"choice","stem":"把下列句子排成一段通顺的话，顺序正确的是：①因此，我们要节约用水。②水是生命之源。③如果没有水，动植物都无法生存。④然而，地球上的淡水资源非常有限。","options":["②③④①","①②③④","②④③①","③②④①"],"answer":0,"explain":"先立论（②水是生命之源）→ 反面说明（③没水无法生存）→ 转折（④淡水有限）→ 结论（①所以要节约）。「因此」「然而」是判断顺序的路标。"}],"output":{"type":"复盘","title":"写一张「本周错题清单」","prompt":"把 Day 1–6 的错题按科目抄成三列：题号 / 错在哪一步 / 正确做法一句话。只写「我为什么错」，不要抄整道题。","checklist":["三科都有记录（没有就写「无」）","每条都写了原因","原因具体到步骤，不是「粗心」两个字","明天早读前读一遍"]}},{"day":8,"title":"人物类记叙文：从做法看性格","minutes":34,"focus":["主谓一致","人物性格推断","因数与倍数"],"warmup":"人物题不要选形容词本身，要选「哪件事说明她是什么样的人」。每题找出一件具体的事做依据。","passage":{"title":"The Girl Who Loved Numbers","text":"Katherine Johnson was born in 1918 in a small town in West Virginia. She loved numbers. By the time she was ten, she had finished all the math her school could teach her.\n\nIn those years, many schools did not let black students study with white students. Katherine's family drove hundreds of miles so that she could go to a better school.\n\nLater, she worked for NASA. She calculated the paths that rockets would follow. In 1962, an astronaut named John Glenn was about to orbit the Earth. The computer gave an answer, but he did not trust it. \"Get the girl to check the numbers,\" he said. She did, and the numbers were right.\n\nKatherine worked at NASA for 33 years. She said she was never afraid of hard problems — only of not trying.","note":"读人物传记时，把「她做了什么」和「这说明她怎样」分成两栏记。"},"questions":[{"subject":"eng","skill":"主谓一致","type":"choice","stem":"There ______ a book and two pens on the desk.","options":["is","are","be","have"],"answer":0,"explain":"There be 句型遵循「就近原则」：离 be 最近的是 a book（单数），所以用 is。"},{"subject":"eng","skill":"主谓一致","type":"choice","stem":"Each of the students ______ a school uniform.","options":["have","has","having","were"],"answer":1,"explain":"each of + 复数名词，谓语仍用单数：has。同类还有 every one of、none of（正式用法）。"},{"subject":"eng","skill":"人物推断","type":"reading","stem":"Which sentence best describes Katherine?","options":["She was talented but lazy.","She was determined and good at math.","She was afraid of computers.","She wanted to become an astronaut."],"answer":1,"explain":"十岁学完学校的数学（天赋）+ 全家驱车数百里去更好的学校（决心）。两项证据合起来选 B。"},{"subject":"eng","skill":"细节","type":"reading","stem":"Why did Katherine's family drive hundreds of miles?","options":["To visit her grandparents.","So that she could attend a better school.","To find work in another town.","To meet John Glenn."],"answer":1,"explain":"第二段原句：so that she could go to a better school。so that 引出目的。"},{"subject":"eng","skill":"写作意图","type":"reading","stem":"Why does the writer include John Glenn's words?","options":["To show that computers were useless.","To show that people trusted Katherine's work.","To explain how rockets fly.","To prove that Glenn was famous."],"answer":1,"explain":"「让那个姑娘核对数字」→ 说明她的计算比机器更被信任。引用人物原话，通常是为了证明这个人的能力或品质。"},{"subject":"math","skill":"因数","type":"choice","stem":"Which number is a factor of 36?","options":["5","7","8","9"],"answer":3,"explain":"36 ÷ 9 = 4，能整除，所以 9 是 36 的因数。5、7、8 都不能整除 36。"},{"subject":"math","skill":"多位数乘法","type":"choice","stem":"306 × 24 = ?","options":["6,144","7,344","7,244","7,444"],"answer":1,"explain":"306 × 20 = 6,120；306 × 4 = 1,224；合计 7,344。中间有 0 时不要漏位。"},{"subject":"math","skill":"整除","type":"choice","stem":"Which number can be divided by BOTH 2 and 5 with no remainder?","options":["25","30","35","45"],"answer":1,"explain":"能被 2 整除 → 个位是偶数；能被 5 整除 → 个位是 0 或 5。同时满足只有个位 0，即 30。"},{"subject":"chi","skill":"修辞","type":"choice","stem":"「春风像一双温柔的手，抚摸着大地。」这句话用了什么修辞手法？","options":["比喻和拟人","排比","夸张","反问"],"answer":0,"explain":"「像……手」是比喻；「抚摸」把春风当人来写，是拟人。一句话里两种修辞并存很常见。"},{"subject":"chi","skill":"成语","type":"choice","stem":"「不耻下问」的意思是：","options":["不好意思向别人提问","向学问或地位不如自己的人请教也不觉得羞耻","不愿意向别人请教","专门问很难的问题"],"answer":1,"explain":"「下」指地位、学问在自己之下。这个成语重点在「不觉得羞耻」，形容谦虚好学。"}],"output":{"type":"口语","title":"介绍一个你佩服的人","prompt":"英文 60 秒：这个人是谁、他做过哪一件具体的事、这件事说明他是什么样的人、你想学他哪一点。","checklist":["有一件具体的事，不是形容词堆砌","用了 because 或 that shows","时态统一（过去的事用过去时）","结尾有一句自己的感受"]}},{"day":9,"title":"观点类文章：找出作者的立场","minutes":34,"focus":["连词","作者立场","分数与周长"],"warmup":"看到 however、but、in fact 就用笔圈起来——作者真正的态度往往在这些词后面。","passage":{"title":"The Plastic Bag Problem","text":"Every minute, people around the world use about one million plastic bags. Most of them are used for only 15 minutes, but they can stay in the environment for hundreds of years.\n\nPlastic bags do not break down like food or paper. Sunlight makes them brittle, and they break into tiny pieces called microplastics. Fish and birds sometimes eat these pieces by mistake. Scientists have found microplastics in rivers, in the sea, and even in rain.\n\nSome countries have passed laws to stop shops from giving out free plastic bags. In Rwanda, plastic bags have been banned since 2008, and the streets are much cleaner.\n\nBut the best solution is simpler: bring your own bag. One cloth bag, used every day for a year, can replace more than 300 plastic ones.","note":"数字在这类文章里是论据：15 分钟 vs 几百年、1 个布袋 vs 300 个塑料袋，都是在制造对比。"},"questions":[{"subject":"eng","skill":"连词","type":"choice","stem":"I stayed at home ______ it was raining heavily.","options":["so","because","but","although"],"answer":1,"explain":"后句是原因（下大雨），前句是结果（待在家），用 because。so 的方向相反。"},{"subject":"eng","skill":"连词","type":"choice","stem":"______ he was very tired, he finished all his homework.","options":["Because","Although","So","And"],"answer":1,"explain":"「累」和「还是完成了」是让步关系，用 Although（虽然）。注意 although 不能和 but 同时用。"},{"subject":"eng","skill":"作者目的","type":"reading","stem":"What is the writer's main purpose?","options":["To sell cloth bags to readers.","To explain a problem and suggest a solution.","To describe how plastic is made.","To compare shopping habits in different countries."],"answer":1,"explain":"前两段讲问题（用量大、难降解、进入食物链），后两段讲办法（立法、自带布袋）。"},{"subject":"eng","skill":"词义","type":"reading","stem":"What are \"microplastics\"?","options":["Very small bags used in shops","Tiny pieces that plastic breaks into","A kind of fish food","New bags made from paper"],"answer":1,"explain":"原文：they break into tiny pieces called microplastics。micro = 微小，直接对应 tiny pieces。"},{"subject":"eng","skill":"论据作用","type":"reading","stem":"Why does the writer mention Rwanda?","options":["To give an example of a law that worked.","To show that Rwanda makes plastic bags.","To compare rainfall in two countries.","To prove that cloth bags are expensive."],"answer":0,"explain":"Rwanda 是「立法禁用塑料袋」的实例，后面紧跟结果 the streets are much cleaner —— 用来证明办法有效。"},{"subject":"math","skill":"分数应用","type":"choice","stem":"A class has 24 students. Three eighths of them walk to school. How many students walk?","options":["6","8","9","12"],"answer":2,"explain":"先求 1/8：24 ÷ 8 = 3；再乘 3：3 × 3 = 9。分数应用题先除后乘，顺序别反。"},{"subject":"math","skill":"三角形周长","type":"choice","stem":"A triangle has sides of 5 cm, 5 cm and 8 cm. What is its perimeter?","options":["18 cm","13 cm","40 cm","20 cm"],"answer":0,"explain":"周长 = 三边之和 = 5 + 5 + 8 = 18 cm。这是等腰三角形，两条腰相等。"},{"subject":"math","skill":"小数减法","type":"choice","stem":"10 − 3.45 = ?","options":["6.55","7.55","6.45","7.45"],"answer":0,"explain":"把 10 写成 10.00，再减：10.00 − 3.45 = 6.55。退位时容易出错，建议列竖式。"},{"subject":"chi","skill":"成语运用","type":"choice","stem":"下列句子中成语使用恰当的一项是：","options":["他遇到难题总是不耻下问，跑去请教老师。","运动会上，同学们争先恐后地冲向终点。","这道题很简单，他想了半天才恍然大悟。","教室里鸦雀无声，同学们正在热烈讨论。"],"answer":1,"explain":"A「下问」指问不如自己的人，向老师请教用错；C「简单」与「想了半天」矛盾；D「鸦雀无声」与「热烈讨论」矛盾。"},{"subject":"chi","skill":"缩句","type":"choice","stem":"把「美丽的小鸟在枝头快乐地唱歌。」缩句，最恰当的是：","options":["小鸟唱歌。","美丽的小鸟唱歌。","小鸟在枝头。","小鸟快乐地唱歌。"],"answer":0,"explain":"缩句保留「谁 + 做什么」，去掉所有修饰语（美丽的、在枝头、快乐地）。主干是「小鸟唱歌」。"}],"output":{"type":"写作","title":"英文观点段：该不该禁止塑料袋","prompt":"用 5 句话写你的立场：观点 → 理由 1 → 理由 2 → 可能有人反对（However…）→ 结论。不超过 70 词。","checklist":["第一句明确表态","用了 However 引出对立面","两个理由不重复","结论句和第一句呼应但换了说法"]}},{"day":10,"title":"工程类说明文：数字与对比","minutes":35,"focus":["情态动词","说明文结构","角度与对称"],"warmup":"这类文章要边读边画：三种桥各画一个简图，标上受力方向。图记住了，题就答得快。","passage":{"title":"Why Bridges Do Not Fall Down","text":"Look at a bridge and you may wonder: why doesn't it fall? The answer is that a bridge must carry two kinds of load — its own weight and the weight of everything crossing it.\n\nThere are three main kinds of bridges. A beam bridge is the simplest: a flat piece lying on two supports. It is cheap, but it can only cross short distances. An arch bridge curves upward, so the weight pushes down and out into the ground on both sides. A suspension bridge hangs from long cables, which is why it can cross very wide rivers.\n\nEngineers test models in wind tunnels before they build. Even so, bridges can fail. In 1940, a bridge in Washington State shook in the wind and fell apart only four months after it opened. Since then, engineers have studied that failure carefully, and modern bridges are much safer.","note":"三种桥的差别只有一个问题：重量往哪里传。抓住这一点，细节题全部能定位。"},"questions":[{"subject":"eng","skill":"情态动词","type":"choice","stem":"You ______ wear a helmet when you ride a bike. It is the rule.","options":["can","must","might","could"],"answer":1,"explain":"It is the rule 说明是「必须」，用 must。can 表示能力或许可，might/could 表示可能性。"},{"subject":"eng","skill":"情态动词","type":"choice","stem":"______ I borrow your pencil, please?","options":["May","Must","Should","Need"],"answer":0,"explain":"请求许可用 May I…?（比 Can I 更礼貌）。Must I…? 是「我必须吗」，意思完全不同。"},{"subject":"eng","skill":"主旨","type":"reading","stem":"What is the passage mainly about?","options":["The history of one famous bridge.","Kinds of bridges and how they carry weight.","How to build a model bridge at home.","Why rivers are difficult to cross."],"answer":1,"explain":"第一段讲「桥要承受两种重量」，第二段分类讲三种桥，合起来就是 B。"},{"subject":"eng","skill":"细节","type":"reading","stem":"Why can a suspension bridge cross very wide rivers?","options":["It is made of wood.","It hangs from long cables.","It has no weight.","It floats on the water."],"answer":1,"explain":"原句：A suspension bridge hangs from long cables, which is why it can cross very wide rivers。which 指代前半句。"},{"subject":"eng","skill":"论据作用","type":"reading","stem":"Why does the writer mention the bridge that fell in 1940?","options":["To show that engineers learn from failures.","To prove that wind tunnels are useless.","To explain how to build a bridge.","To describe the weather in Washington."],"answer":0,"explain":"后一句紧接：Since then, engineers have studied that failure carefully, and modern bridges are much safer。"},{"subject":"math","skill":"三角形内角和","type":"choice","stem":"Two angles of a triangle are 45° and 65°. What is the third angle?","options":["70°","80°","90°","110°"],"answer":0,"explain":"三角形内角和 180°：180 − 45 − 65 = 70°。"},{"subject":"math","skill":"对称轴","type":"choice","stem":"How many lines of symmetry does a square have?","options":["1","2","4","8"],"answer":2,"explain":"正方形有 4 条对称轴：2 条对边中点连线 + 2 条对角线。"},{"subject":"math","skill":"周长逆推","type":"choice","stem":"A rectangle has a perimeter of 30 cm and a length of 9 cm. What is its width?","options":["6 cm","12 cm","21 cm","15 cm"],"answer":0,"explain":"长 + 宽 = 30 ÷ 2 = 15；宽 = 15 − 9 = 6 cm。先除以 2 是关键一步，直接用 30 − 9 就错了。"},{"subject":"chi","skill":"比喻","type":"choice","stem":"下列句子中，没有使用比喻的一项是：","options":["月亮像一只小船挂在天空。","他跑得像一阵风。","弟弟长得很像爸爸。","树叶像蝴蝶一样飘落下来。"],"answer":2,"explain":"「长得像」是同类事物之间的比较，不是比喻。比喻要求本体和喻体是不同类的事物。"},{"subject":"chi","skill":"古诗","type":"choice","stem":"「谁知盘中餐，粒粒皆辛苦」出自哪首诗？","options":["《静夜思》","《悯农》","《春晓》","《咏鹅》"],"answer":1,"explain":"李绅《悯农》：锄禾日当午，汗滴禾下土。谁知盘中餐，粒粒皆辛苦。"}],"output":{"type":"口语","title":"用英文解释一个「为什么」","prompt":"选一个生活现象（为什么船不会沉 / 为什么天空是蓝的 / 为什么要睡觉），用 60 秒讲清楚：先给答案，再给两个原因。","checklist":["开头第一句就给答案","用了 because / that is why","两个原因不重复","被追问「还有呢」时能再补一句"]}},{"day":11,"title":"双面观点文：把两边都读完","minutes":35,"focus":["现在进行时","正反观点文","价格应用题"],"warmup":"这类文章一半支持、一半反对。读的时候画一条竖线，左边写 for，右边写 against，最后再看作者的落点。","passage":{"title":"Should Students Wear Uniforms?","text":"Every morning, students at Willow School put on the same blue shirt and grey trousers. Some of them hate it. Others say it makes life easier.\n\nThose who support uniforms give three reasons. First, students do not have to decide what to wear, so mornings are faster. Second, uniforms make everyone look equal: a student from a rich family and a student from a poor family wear exactly the same thing. Third, when a class goes on a trip, teachers can find their students in a crowd in seconds.\n\nThose who are against uniforms say something different. Clothes are a way to show who you are, they argue. A child who loves art may want to wear bright colours; a child who plays basketball may want to wear a team shirt. Taking that choice away, they say, does not make school fairer — it just makes school quieter.\n\nMost students at Willow School have made up their minds. The question is which side their parents are on.","note":"注意最后一段没有给结论 —— 这是作者故意留白，也是一种写作手法。"},"questions":[{"subject":"eng","skill":"现在进行时","type":"choice","stem":"Look! The children ______ in the garden.","options":["play","plays","are playing","played"],"answer":2,"explain":"Look! 是现在进行时的信号词，结构 be + 动词-ing：are playing。"},{"subject":"eng","skill":"一般现在时","type":"choice","stem":"My father ______ coffee every morning.","options":["drink","drinks","is drinking","drinking"],"answer":1,"explain":"every morning 表示习惯，用一般现在时；主语 My father 是第三人称单数 → drinks。"},{"subject":"eng","skill":"主旨","type":"reading","stem":"What is the passage mainly about?","options":["Why Willow School is the best school.","Arguments for and against school uniforms.","How to choose clothes in the morning.","Why teachers like school trips."],"answer":1,"explain":"第二段写支持方三条理由，第三段写反对方理由，全文是「正反并列」。"},{"subject":"eng","skill":"细节","type":"reading","stem":"According to supporters, what is ONE advantage of uniforms?","options":["They are cheaper than other clothes.","Teachers can find students easily on trips.","They keep students warm in winter.","They help students make friends."],"answer":1,"explain":"第三点：teachers can find their students in a crowd in seconds。注意题干 ONE advantage，只要找到一条即可。"},{"subject":"eng","skill":"观点识别","type":"reading","stem":"What do people who are AGAINST uniforms believe?","options":["Clothes are a way to show who you are.","Uniforms make mornings too slow.","Uniforms cost too much money.","Students should wear the same clothes."],"answer":0,"explain":"第三段首句：Clothes are a way to show who you are, they argue。argue 后面就是他们的核心观点。"},{"subject":"math","skill":"总价","type":"choice","stem":"Each notebook costs $2.50. How much do 4 notebooks cost?","options":["$7.50","$10.00","$12.50","$8.50"],"answer":1,"explain":"总价 = 单价 × 数量 = 2.50 × 4 = $10.00。"},{"subject":"math","skill":"找零","type":"choice","stem":"You pay $20 for a book that costs $13.75. How much change do you get?","options":["$6.25","$7.25","$6.75","$7.75"],"answer":0,"explain":"20.00 − 13.75 = 6.25。可以用「补到 20」的方法：13.75 → 14（0.25）→ 20（6），合计 6.25。"},{"subject":"math","skill":"两位数除法","type":"choice","stem":"425 ÷ 17 = ?","options":["24","25","26","35"],"answer":1,"explain":"17 × 25 = 425（17 × 100 ÷ 4 = 425）。验算最快：17 × 25 = 17 × 20 + 17 × 5 = 340 + 85 = 425。"},{"subject":"chi","skill":"近义词辨析","type":"choice","stem":"教室里很（　），同学们都在认真做题。","options":["宁静","安静","平静","幽静"],"answer":1,"explain":"「安静」指没有声音，适合形容教室、病房；「宁静」多形容夜晚、乡村的氛围；「平静」形容心情或水面；「幽静」形容幽深僻静的地方。"},{"subject":"chi","skill":"短文理解","type":"choice","stem":"读这段话：「小松鼠把松果一颗一颗搬进树洞。它来来回回跑了二十多趟，直到树洞再也装不下。冬天来了，大雪盖住了整片森林。小松鼠坐在洞口，慢慢地吃着自己的松果。」这段话主要写了什么？","options":["小松鼠怎样为冬天做准备","森林里的雪下得很大","松果的味道很好","小松鼠很喜欢玩耍"],"answer":0,"explain":"「搬松果—跑二十多趟—装不下」都在写准备过程，后半段是结果。B、C、D 都只是文中的零碎信息，不是主要内容。"}],"output":{"type":"写作","title":"给校长写一封英文短信","prompt":"写 6–8 句给校长，提出一个改善学校的建议（例如延长图书馆开放时间）。格式：Dear Principal, → 我是谁 → 建议是什么 → 两个理由 → 感谢 → Yours, 名字。","checklist":["有称呼和结尾","建议具体到「做什么」","两个理由各一句","没有一句超过 15 个词"]}},{"day":12,"title":"记叙文：环境描写在暗示什么","minutes":35,"focus":["将来时","环境与情绪","行程与时间"],"warmup":"好的记叙文里，天气、光线、声音都不是随便写的。今天每读完一段，问一句：这段在制造什么感觉？","passage":{"title":"The Cave at the End of the Beach","text":"The tide was going out, and the beach was wider than Lila had ever seen it. Far down by the rocks, a dark opening appeared — a cave she had never noticed before.\n\n\"Ten minutes,\" her father said. \"And we stay together.\"\n\nInside, the air was cool and smelled of salt. Lila's footsteps echoed. On the wall she saw lines of tiny shells, pressed into the stone like writing. Her father explained that the sea had put them there, one layer at a time, over thousands of years.\n\nThen a sound: a low, steady rush. Water was coming back in.\n\nThey walked out quickly, and the cave grew smaller behind them. By the time they reached the dry sand, the opening was gone. Lila looked back at the flat grey sea and felt, for the first time, that the ocean was not a place but a living thing with its own schedule.","note":"标出所有写「声音」和「光」的句子：echoed、a low steady rush、flat grey sea。"},"questions":[{"subject":"eng","skill":"一般将来时","type":"choice","stem":"We ______ visit the science museum next Friday.","options":["will","are","did","have"],"answer":0,"explain":"next Friday 表示将来，用 will + 动词原形。"},{"subject":"eng","skill":"be going to","type":"choice","stem":"Look at those dark clouds! It ______ rain.","options":["rains","is going to","rained","rain"],"answer":1,"explain":"有明确迹象（乌云）的预测用 be going to；will 更多用于临时决定或单纯预测。"},{"subject":"eng","skill":"因果","type":"reading","stem":"Why did the cave disappear?","options":["The rocks fell down.","The tide came back in.","Lila and her father moved away.","It became dark."],"answer":1,"explain":"前文伏笔：The tide was going out；后文 Water was coming back in。涨潮把洞口淹没了。"},{"subject":"eng","skill":"细节","type":"reading","stem":"What did Lila see on the wall of the cave?","options":["A drawing made by other visitors.","Lines of tiny shells pressed into the stone.","A map of the beach.","Her own shadow."],"answer":1,"explain":"原句：lines of tiny shells, pressed into the stone like writing。"},{"subject":"eng","skill":"句意推断","type":"reading","stem":"What does the LAST sentence suggest about Lila?","options":["She is afraid of the sea.","She now sees the ocean as powerful and alive.","She wants to become a scientist.","She is angry with her father."],"answer":1,"explain":"not a place but a living thing with its own schedule —— 她第一次感到海是「有生命、有自己的时间表」的。"},{"subject":"math","skill":"行程","type":"choice","stem":"A train travels 60 km every hour. How far does it travel in 3.5 hours?","options":["180 km","200 km","210 km","240 km"],"answer":2,"explain":"路程 = 速度 × 时间 = 60 × 3.5 = 210 km。（60 × 3 = 180，60 × 0.5 = 30，合计 210）"},{"subject":"math","skill":"单位时间产量","type":"choice","stem":"A machine makes 25 bottles every minute. How many bottles does it make in one hour?","options":["250","600","1,500","2,500"],"answer":2,"explain":"1 小时 = 60 分钟，25 × 60 = 1,500。先换算单位，再乘。"},{"subject":"math","skill":"时间换算","type":"choice","stem":"A film lasts 135 minutes. How long is that in hours and minutes?","options":["1 hour 35 minutes","2 hours 15 minutes","2 hours 35 minutes","3 hours 15 minutes"],"answer":1,"explain":"135 ÷ 60 = 2 余 15，即 2 小时 15 分钟。"},{"subject":"chi","skill":"名句","type":"choice","stem":"「读书破万卷，下笔如有神」的作者是：","options":["李白","杜甫","白居易","王维"],"answer":1,"explain":"出自杜甫《奉赠韦左丞丈二十二韵》，意思是书读得多，写起来就得心应手。"},{"subject":"chi","skill":"字义","type":"choice","stem":"「迫不及待」中「及」的意思是：","options":["及格","来得及","达到","和"],"answer":1,"explain":"「不及」即「来不及」。整个成语形容急迫得不能再等待。"}],"output":{"type":"口语","title":"复述一个故事","prompt":"读完今天的文章，合上屏幕，用英文复述 90 秒：谁、去哪、看到什么、发生什么、最后怎样。要求用 3 个原文里的细节。","checklist":["有完整五要素","用了至少 3 个原文细节","时态统一为过去时","结尾有一句自己的感受"]}},{"day":13,"title":"科普说明文：数字背后的比较","minutes":35,"focus":["标点与所有格","数字信息题","规律推理"],"warmup":"科普文里的数字几乎必考。读到数字就圈出来，旁边写一句「和什么比」。","passage":{"title":"A Year on Mars","text":"On Earth, a year lasts 365 days. On Mars, it lasts 687 Earth days — almost twice as long. That is because Mars is farther from the Sun, so it moves more slowly along its path.\n\nA day on Mars is called a \"sol.\" It is only about 40 minutes longer than a day on Earth, which is why engineers who drive Mars rovers set their watches to Mars time. Some of them live on a schedule that shifts a little every day.\n\nMars is also much colder. Its average temperature is about −60°C, and the air is very thin — mostly carbon dioxide. There is water, but it is frozen in the ground and at the poles.\n\nStill, people keep planning to go. A trip would take about seven months, and the first astronauts would have to grow food, make oxygen, and repair their own machines, far from any help.","note":"数字题注意「和谁比」：687 是地球日，不是火星日；40 分钟是「一天」的差，不是「一年」的差。"},"questions":[{"subject":"eng","skill":"标点","type":"choice","stem":"Choose the sentence with correct punctuation.","options":["\"Where are you going\" asked Tom.","\"Where are you going?\" asked Tom.","\"Where are you going\"? asked Tom.","\"Where are you going,\" asked Tom?"],"answer":1,"explain":"直接引语是问句，问号放在引号内，引号外不再加问号。"},{"subject":"eng","skill":"所有格","type":"choice","stem":"This is ______ book. (The book belongs to the girl.)","options":["the girls","the girl's","the girls'","the girl"],"answer":1,"explain":"单数名词所有格加 's：the girl's book。the girls' 是复数所有格（多个女孩共有的）。"},{"subject":"eng","skill":"因果","type":"reading","stem":"Why is a year on Mars longer than a year on Earth?","options":["Mars spins faster.","Mars is farther from the Sun and moves more slowly.","Mars has two moons.","Mars is colder than Earth."],"answer":1,"explain":"原句：That is because Mars is farther from the Sun, so it moves more slowly along its path。"},{"subject":"eng","skill":"词义","type":"reading","stem":"What is a \"sol\"?","options":["A day on Mars","A year on Mars","A kind of robot","A month on Earth"],"answer":0,"explain":"第二段首句直接定义：A day on Mars is called a \"sol.\" 后面还拿它和地球的一天比长短。"},{"subject":"eng","skill":"推断","type":"reading","stem":"Why would the first astronauts on Mars need many different skills?","options":["They would be bored.","There would be no one nearby to help them.","They would have to teach children.","Mars has too many rocks."],"answer":1,"explain":"末句：grow food, make oxygen, and repair their own machines, far from any help —— 远离援助，只能自己来。"},{"subject":"math","skill":"规律","type":"choice","stem":"What number comes next? 3, 7, 15, 31, ___","options":["47","55","63","62"],"answer":2,"explain":"规律是「×2 + 1」：3×2+1=7，7×2+1=15，15×2+1=31，31×2+1=63。也可以看差：+4、+8、+16、+32。"},{"subject":"math","skill":"规律","type":"choice","stem":"What number comes next? 2, 6, 12, 20, 30, ___","options":["36","40","42","45"],"answer":2,"explain":"相邻两数的差依次是 4、6、8、10，下一个差是 12：30 + 12 = 42。"},{"subject":"math","skill":"逻辑推理","type":"choice","stem":"Tom, Amy and Ben each have a different pet: a cat, a dog or a fish. Tom's pet does not have fins. Amy's pet barks. Who has the fish?","options":["Tom","Amy","Ben","It cannot be decided"],"answer":2,"explain":"Amy 的宠物会叫 → 狗；Tom 的宠物没有鳍 → 不是鱼，只能是猫；剩下 Ben 是鱼。做这类题画表格，一人一行逐一排除。"},{"subject":"chi","skill":"标点","type":"choice","stem":"下列句子中，冒号使用正确的一项是：","options":["他喜欢三种水果：苹果、香蕉和梨。","他喜欢：苹果、香蕉和梨。","他喜欢三种水果，苹果、香蕉和梨。","他：喜欢三种水果，苹果、香蕉和梨。"],"answer":0,"explain":"冒号用在总说之后、分说之前，且要管到句末。B 缺少总说部分，C、D 位置或搭配不当。"},{"subject":"chi","skill":"短文理解","type":"choice","stem":"读这段话：「外婆的手很粗糙，指节上有一层薄薄的茧。她总说自己的手不好看，可她用这双手包出的粽子，棱角分明，一根线也不松。每年端午，邻居家的孩子都会跑来，趴在灶台边等。」这段话主要想表达什么？","options":["外婆包的粽子特别好吃，孩子们都爱吃","外婆的手虽然粗糙，却很能干，让人感到温暖","外婆不喜欢自己的手","端午节有吃粽子的习俗"],"answer":1,"explain":"「粗糙/茧」和「棱角分明/孩子趴在灶台边等」形成对照，落点在「手不好看但很能干、很温暖」。A 只是表层，C 是文中一句反衬，D 是背景。"}],"output":{"type":"写作","title":"英文续写：给故事加一个结尾","prompt":"用 6 句话给下面这个故事写结尾：「Sam found a key under the old bridge. It was warm, as if someone had just held it…」要求：交代钥匙是谁的、Sam 做了什么决定、最后一句话留下余味。","checklist":["用过去时叙述","至少 1 句对话","结尾不是「然后他回家了」","检查每句是否有主语和动词"]}},{"day":14,"title":"全真模考：英语 25 分钟 + 数学 15 分钟","minutes":45,"focus":["跨题型","时间分配","一次做对"],"warmup":"今天完全模拟考场：先计时做英语部分（1–5 题），再做数学（6–8），最后语文。中途不查答案、不休息。","passage":{"title":"The Man Who Planted a Forest","text":"In 1979, a teenager named Jadav Payeng was walking along a sandy riverbank in Assam, India. A flood had washed away many trees, and hundreds of snakes had died in the heat. He could not forget what he saw.\n\nHe decided to plant one tree every day. At first it was only bamboo. He carried water from the river, watered each plant by hand, and kept animals away. People laughed at him. \"Nothing will grow here,\" they said.\n\nHe kept planting. After ten years, there was a small wood. After twenty, animals began to arrive — deer, birds, and later elephants. After nearly forty years, the place had become a forest of about 550 hectares, larger than 700 football fields.\n\nToday the forest is called Molai Wood, after his nickname. Foresters say it is one of the largest forests ever planted by a single person.","note":"先扫一遍题干，带着问题读。文学性细节可以跳过，数字和时间线必须抓住。"},"questions":[{"subject":"eng","skill":"句子合并","type":"choice","stem":"Choose the BEST way to combine the two sentences: \"The boy was tired. He finished his homework.\"","options":["The boy was tired, but he finished his homework.","The boy was tired, so he finished his homework.","Although the boy was tired, but he finished his homework.","The boy was tired because he finished his homework."],"answer":0,"explain":"前后是转折关系（累，但还是完成了），用 but。C 中 Although 与 but 不能同时使用；B、D 逻辑颠倒。"},{"subject":"eng","skill":"代词","type":"choice","stem":"Which sentence is written correctly?","options":["Me and my friend went to the zoo.","My friend and me went to the zoo.","My friend and I went to the zoo.","I and my friend went to the zoo."],"answer":2,"explain":"作主语用主格 I；英语习惯把「我」放在后面：My friend and I。"},{"subject":"eng","skill":"起因","type":"reading","stem":"Why did Jadav decide to start planting trees?","options":["He wanted to become famous.","He was deeply moved by the dead snakes and the damaged land.","The government asked him to.","He needed wood to sell."],"answer":1,"explain":"第一段：flood 冲走树木、数百条蛇热死，He could not forget what he saw —— 触动他的是目睹的景象。"},{"subject":"eng","skill":"时间线","type":"reading","stem":"About how long did it take before animals began to arrive?","options":["Ten years","Twenty years","Forty years","Seven years"],"answer":1,"explain":"第三段：After twenty, animals began to arrive。十年是「小树林」，四十年是「森林成型」，三个时间点要分清。"},{"subject":"eng","skill":"写作意图","type":"reading","stem":"What does the writer most want readers to feel?","options":["That planting trees is boring work.","That one person's persistence can change a whole landscape.","That floods are the most dangerous natural disaster.","That India has more forests than other countries."],"answer":1,"explain":"全文用「一个人 × 四十年 × 550 公顷」的对比，结尾强调 planted by a single person —— 落点在个人坚持的力量。"},{"subject":"math","skill":"混合运算","type":"choice","stem":"480 ÷ 8 + 15 × 6 = ?","options":["150","180","240","105"],"answer":0,"explain":"先乘除：480 ÷ 8 = 60，15 × 6 = 90；再相加：60 + 90 = 150。"},{"subject":"math","skill":"面积与总价","type":"choice","stem":"A rectangular room is 6 m long and 4 m wide. Carpet costs $12 per square metre. What is the total cost?","options":["$120","$240","$288","$144"],"answer":2,"explain":"面积 = 6 × 4 = 24 m²；总价 = 24 × 12 = $288。这类题两步，别停在面积就选答案。"},{"subject":"math","skill":"异分母分数加法","type":"choice","stem":"2/3 + 1/6 = ?","options":["3/9","5/6","3/6","1/2"],"answer":1,"explain":"通分：2/3 = 4/6，4/6 + 1/6 = 5/6。分母不同的分数不能直接加分子。"},{"subject":"chi","skill":"字形","type":"choice","stem":"下列词语书写完全正确的一项是：","options":["专心致志","全神惯注","迫不急待","再所不辞"],"answer":0,"explain":"应为：全神贯注（贯，集中）、迫不及待（及）、在所不辞（在）。"},{"subject":"chi","skill":"短文理解","type":"choice","stem":"读这段话：「爸爸把车停在路边，蹲下来替我把鞋带系好。他什么也没说，只是拍了拍我的肩。我上车的时候，从后视镜里看见他还站在原地，一直看着车开远。」这段文字主要表现了什么？","options":["爸爸很会系鞋带","爸爸对「我」的关心和不舍","路上的车很多","「我」自己不会系鞋带"],"answer":1,"explain":"「蹲下来系鞋带」「什么也没说」「站在原地一直看」三个动作细节，都在写不说出口的关心。做这类题要找「动作」，不要停在字面。"}],"output":{"type":"复盘","title":"模考复盘：写三句话给自己","prompt":"合上题目，写三句话：①今天最不该错的一题是什么；②时间够不够，卡在哪一部分；③明天只做哪一件事。","checklist":["三句都写具体，不写「加油」","指出卡住的具体题型","明天的任务不超过 1 件"]}},{"day":15,"title":"收尾：只做错题 + 面试实战","minutes":40,"focus":["错题回顾","面试口述","心态调整"],"warmup":"今天不刷新题。把错题本从头翻一遍，每道题让孩子讲给你听；然后完整走一遍面试流程。","passage":{"title":"The Cracked Pot","text":"A water carrier had two pots. One was perfect; the other had a small crack. Every day, the cracked pot arrived home only half full.\n\nFor two years, the pot felt ashamed. Finally it said, \"I am sorry. Because of my crack, you have to walk back for more water.\"\n\nThe carrier smiled. \"Did you notice the flowers on your side of the path? I planted seeds there, and every day you watered them. Because of your crack, I have flowers on my table. Without it, I would have nothing.\"\n\nThe pot never felt ashamed again.","note":"寓言题的答案通常在最后一句「反转」里。先找反转，再想道理。"},"questions":[{"subject":"eng","skill":"综合改错","type":"choice","stem":"Which sentence has NO mistake?","options":["She don't like apples.","She doesn't likes apples.","She doesn't like apples.","She not like apples."],"answer":2,"explain":"第三人称单数否定：doesn't + 动词原形。doesn't 已经承担了三单变化，后面的动词不能再加 s。"},{"subject":"eng","skill":"疑问句","type":"choice","stem":"Choose the correct question.","options":["Where you are going?","Where are you going?","Where do you going?","Where you go?"],"answer":1,"explain":"含 be 动词的疑问句直接倒装：Where are you going? do/does 用于实义动词，不能和 going 连用。"},{"subject":"eng","skill":"因果","type":"reading","stem":"Why did the cracked pot feel ashamed?","options":["It was made of cheap clay.","It could only carry half the water home.","The other pot laughed at it.","It was left outside at night."],"answer":1,"explain":"首段：the cracked pot arrived home only half full；第二段它道歉说「因为我漏水，你得来回多走一趟」。"},{"subject":"eng","skill":"推理","type":"reading","stem":"Why did the carrier plant seeds on ONE side of the path?","options":["He wanted to sell the flowers.","He knew the cracked pot would water that side.","That side had better soil.","He forgot to plant the other side."],"answer":1,"explain":"「每天你给它们浇水」—— 他早就知道裂缝会漏水，是故意利用这一点。这是全文的巧思。"},{"subject":"eng","skill":"寓意","type":"reading","stem":"What is the lesson of this story?","options":["Broken things should be thrown away.","A weakness can still be useful in the right place.","Water is more valuable than flowers.","We should always carry two pots."],"answer":1,"explain":"裂缝是「缺点」，却浇出了花 —— 缺点放对位置也能变成价值。寓言题的寓意要能覆盖整个故事，不能只抓一句。"},{"subject":"math","skill":"异分母分数","type":"choice","stem":"1/2 + 1/4 = ?","options":["2/6","3/4","1/6","2/4"],"answer":1,"explain":"1/2 = 2/4，2/4 + 1/4 = 3/4。分子分母同时相加是最典型的错误（得到 2/6）。"},{"subject":"math","skill":"小数减法","type":"choice","stem":"5.6 − 2.78 = ?","options":["2.82","3.82","2.92","3.18"],"answer":0,"explain":"补位：5.60 − 2.78 = 2.82。百分位 0−8 要向前借位。"},{"subject":"math","skill":"速度","type":"choice","stem":"A car travels 240 km in 4 hours. What is its average speed?","options":["40 km/h","60 km/h","80 km/h","960 km/h"],"answer":1,"explain":"速度 = 路程 ÷ 时间 = 240 ÷ 4 = 60 km/h。"},{"subject":"chi","skill":"病句","type":"choice","stem":"下列句子没有语病的一项是：","options":["我们要养成认真完成作业。","他的写作水平明显改进了。","妈妈买回了苹果、香蕉和水果。","这本书我一口气读完了。"],"answer":3,"explain":"A 缺宾语（养成……的习惯）；B 搭配不当（水平应「提高」）；C 分类不当（苹果、香蕉属于水果，不能并列）。"},{"subject":"chi","skill":"短文理解","type":"choice","stem":"读这段话：「竹子前四年只长三厘米，第五年开始，每天长三十厘米，六周就能长到十五米。原来，前四年它把根扎进土里，延伸了数百平方米。」这段话告诉我们什么道理？","options":["竹子是长得最快的植物","前期的积累看起来慢，却决定了后面的高度","种竹子要等五年才有收获","竹子需要很多水"],"answer":1,"explain":"「前四年三厘米」与「六周长十五米」形成强烈对比，最后一句「原来」揭示原因 —— 落点在看不见的积累。"}],"output":{"type":"面试","title":"全套面试模拟（15 分钟）","prompt":"家长扮演面试官，中英文交替提问 8 个问题（可从「资料」页题库随机抽），要求孩子每题回答 3–5 句，不背稿。最后问一句「你觉得自己今天表现怎么样？」","checklist":["每题至少 3 句，不是单词回答","有 1 次主动补充细节","被追问时不慌，能说「Let me think…」","全程有眼神交流，坐姿自然"]}}];
